<title>JAPAN: Strong quake shakes southern Japan.</title>
<headline>Strong quake shakes southern Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong earthquake shook the southern Japanese island of Kyushu on Wednesday, Japan's Meteorological Agency said.  </p>
<p>An agency statement said the earthquake measured 6.2 on the Richter scale, with the epicentre near the city of Kagoshima, 800 km (500 miles) southwest of Tokyo.</p>
<p>There were no immediate reports of any casualties or damage, police said.</p>
